-- title:
--   Hecke translate by s_ℓ matches the d₁ degeneracy leg
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fixed are primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`) and a nonzero level $N$ which is squarefree (`hN`) and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`).
--
--   **Coefficients (`hdvr`–`hunr`, `K₀`).** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), its residue ring has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified lift (`Onr`, `Fr`, `hOnr_complete`–`hFr`).** $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$, $Fr$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of it; $Onr$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the ideal generated by $\pi$ is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation (`vdet`, `hvdet`).** $vdet\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a monoid homomorphism with $vdet\,g=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite side (`hB`, `Λ`, `hΛ`).** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it (`hΛ`).
--
--   **Coarse moduli (`𝒳`, `f`, `pt`, `h𝒳`).** $f\colon\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ together with the point assignment `pt` on fake elliptic curves `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S` (abelian schemes of relative fibre dimension $2$ with commutative relative group law, $\Lambda$-action subject to a trace condition, and level-$N$ data) is a coarse moduli space: `h𝒳` asserts isomorphism invariance, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property.
--
--   **Fine moduli with full level $n$ (`hn`–`hρ`).** $n\ge 3$ is prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; $f_M\colon M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` on pairs $(E,P)$, $P$ a full level-$n$ structure, is a fine moduli space (`hM`: isomorphism invariance, pullback compatibility, surjectivity and injectivity of `ptF` on all base rings). A group $G$ acts by $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$, and `hρ` says this is a level-twist action: each $\rho(g)$ is over the base, twisting a level-$n$ structure by $\chi(g)$ moves `ptF` by $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, unital, surjective and injective modulo $n$.
--
--   **Forgetful map (`p`, `hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`).** $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ lies over the base, is invariant under all $\rho(h)$, and carries `ptF` to `pt`.
--
--   **Hecke tower (`𝒴`, `g`, `ptT`, `h𝒴`, `d₀`, `d₁`, `hd₀f`–`hd₁`).** For each prime $\ell$ distinct from $r,\bar r$ (an element of `HeckeTower.AwayPrime r rbar`), $g_\ell\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptT ℓ` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (`h𝒴`, same five clauses as above). The two degeneracies $d_0(\ell),d_1(\ell)\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ lie over the base; $d_0$ forgets the extra subgroup (`hd₀`), and $d_1$ sends a pair $u$ to any $d$ receiving a level-$\ell$ isogeny from $u$ (`hd₁`).
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner operators (`ar`, `arbar`, `harf`–`harbar`).** $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ lie over the base and carry `pt` of $E$ to `pt` of $E'$ whenever $E'$ is an Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $r$, respectively at $\bar r$.
--
--   **Definite side (`hdef`–`hv`).** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ has $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and is ramified exactly at $\bar r$; $\Lambda_1$ is maximal, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) contained in $\Lambda_1$; $n_1$ is a finite idele in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (it lies in the adelic box of $R_1$, $r\cdot n_1^{-1}$ lies in the box, while neither $n_1^{-1}$ nor $r^{-1}n_1$ does) such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` $=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map into $M_2(K_0)$; $v$ is the height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$.
--
--   **Arithmetic group and Hecke elements (`Γt`, `hΓt`, `s`, `sf`, `hs`, `Γtℓ`, `hΓtℓ`, `wbar`, `hwbar`).** $\Gamma_t$ consists exactly of the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ that are local units of $R_1$ at every place $w\neq v$ (`hΓt`). For each $\ell$, `hs` requires of the pair $(s_\ell,sf_\ell)$: $sf_\ell$ has local component $s_\ell$ at all places not above $r$, component $1$ at places above $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` if $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$. Further $\Gamma_{t,\ell}=\Gamma_t\cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Order coordinates (`hΛℤ`, `coord`, `hcoord`).** All integers lie in $\Lambda$, and `coord` maps $\Lambda$ into $\mathrm{Zp2}(r)\times\mathrm{Zp2}(r)$ (Witt vectors of the quadratic extension of $\mathbb F_r$) additively, unitally, with the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectively, with dense image and with the prescribed trace identity (`hcoord`).
--
--   **Special fibre (`A₀`–`hA₀`).** $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $Onr/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over that ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of $2$-dimensional formal coordinates for $A_0$, and `hA₀` says $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$; $e,e'\colon\Gamma_t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`.
--
--   **Uniformisation of the special fibre (`hE1`–`hE4`, summarised here).** `hE1`: $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ and $e\gamma$ preserves the level structure. `hE1mul`: multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$. `hE1sc`: integral scalars $\gamma=c$ act, up to $r$-powers, as multiplication by $c$. `hE1'`: conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a scalar up to $r$-powers, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar. `hE2`: for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathrm{Zp2}(r)$-action and $\varpi$ of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ is realised on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$. `hE3`: every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ admits a labelling $\Gamma_t\to\Lambda$ realising $e\gamma$ on it, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$. `hE4`: over algebraically closed fields receiving $Onr/(\pi)$, every $r$-power self-isogeny pair preserving the level structure of a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to $r$-powers, from some $e\gamma$.
--
--   **Eichler-order actions (`R₂`–`hE5g`, `Λ₁s`–`hE6f`, summarised here).** $R_2\le R_1$ is an order such that $r$-power multiples of elements of $R_1$ lie in $R_2$, with $\hat e\colon R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base satisfying: compatibility with the group law, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action and preservation of the level structure (`hE5a`); unitality, multiplicativity and agreement with $\Lambda$-multiplication on integers (`hE5b1`–`hE5b3`); $\hat e(\bar x)$ followed by $\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$ (`hE5c`); compatibility with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$ (`hE5d`); a joint normalisation of $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$ by a single $g$ as in `hE2` (`hE5e`); and stability of $R_2$ under the main involution (`hE5g`). Dually, $\Lambda_{1s}$ is a maximal order with $R_1\le\Lambda_{1s}$ and $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_{1s}=R_1$ (`htwin`), $R_2'\le\Lambda_{1s}$ an order with the same $r$-power denominator property, containing $R_2$, and $\hat e'\colon R_2'\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ satisfies the analogous clauses `hE6a`–`hE6c`, extends $\hat e$ (`hE6d`), is star-stable and injective (`hE6e1`, `hE6e2`), and `hE6f` says that if $\hat e'(z)$ kills all $q$-torsion for a prime $q\neq r$ then $r^{K}z\in q\Lambda_{1s}$ for some $K$.
--
--   **Formal moduli package (`ι`–`hE₀`).** $\iota\colon\mathrm{Zp2}(r)\to Onr$; $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$, special relative to $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); $MD$ is a moduli package for $(r,Onr)$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); $\eta$ assigns to rigidified objects points of $MD$, and `hη` has three clauses: on admissible rigidified objects over Noetherian bases $\eta$ identifies exactly the isomorphic ones, $\eta$ commutes with base change, and every point of $MD$ is locally in the image of $\eta$ on admissible objects. $E_0$ embeds the centraliser of the action and $\varpi$ of $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ injectively with image commensurable to $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`.
--
--   **Drinfeld description of $MD$-points (`eD`, `hnatD`–`hPiexD`).** Over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, $eD$ maps the functor of $MD$-points naturally (`hnatD`) and bijectively (`hbijD`) to $(Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(K_0,\pi)(B)$, preserving the $Onr$-leg (`hfstD`); the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` corresponds to the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), $\pi$-translation corresponds to Frobenius twisting of the first coordinate leaving the Deligne datum fixed (`hPiD`), and $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Comparison of formal data (`κ`, `hκ`, `n₀`, `β₀`, `hβ₀`) and the base point `P₀`.** $\kappa$ is compatible with the two quotient maps of $Onr$, $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$, and $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on the special fibre (`A₀w`–`hJOINTw`).** $A_{0w}$ with $a_w,a_w'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $b_w,b_w'$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level structure (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`: a single $g$ simultaneously normalising all $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ as in `hE2` and the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, the latter with $E_0\varepsilon_w=r^{k_w}g\iota_0(\bar w)g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The map $\Xi$ (`Ξ`, `hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef`).** $\Xi$ sends rigidified curves over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to $MD$-points. Over connected bases its $Onr$-leg is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$ (`hΞleg`); it is compatible with pullbacks of rigidifications (`hΞnat`) and invariant under isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated sense (`hΞiso`); and `hΞdef` computes it: over a connected base with $r$ nilpotent, if the curve is a formal module via `coord`, $X$, $\theta$, then there are $j\le1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$, rigidity transport along $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, and $\Xi x=\langle \mathrm{frobTwist}(-j)\psi,\ \eta\,t\rangle$.
--
--   **Equivariance of $\Xi$ (`g₀`, `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`).** There is $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that: translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by the action of $Z^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$, $Z$ the central idele $r$ (`heqΓ`); an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, with the matching correspondence diagram built from $a_w$ followed by $b_w$, moves $\Xi$ by $Z^{c}g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`); and `heqS` states, for any $n_1$, any $\ell$ and any pair $(s,sf)$ satisfying the local conditions of `hs`, and any special-fibre data $C_0,A_{0s},a_s,a_s',b_s,b_s'$ realising the level-$\ell$ isogeny and an $r^{k_s}$-isogeny pair with the joint normalisation `hJOINTs` tied to $\iota_0(\bar s)$: over a Noetherian connected base in which $\ell$ is invertible, if $E'$ is the level-$\ell$ isogeny quotient of $u=(E,C)$ and $\varrho,\varrho'$ are rigidifications linked by the displayed correspondence diagram, then $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ is the $Z^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\ell\,s^{-1})g_0^{-1}$-translate of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ for some $c$.
--
--   **The uniformisation of the fine moduli space (`θt`, `Θf`, `hnat`, `hG`, `hi'`, `het`, `hfib`).** $\theta_t\colon\Gamma_t\to G$ is a group homomorphism, and $\Theta_f$ sends $B$-points of $(Onr\to_{\mathcal O}-)\times\Omega(K_0,\pi)\times G$ to nilpotent points of $f_M$, naturally in $B$ (`hnat`), equivariantly for right translation by $G$ (`hG`), invariantly for the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action combined with left multiplication by $\theta_t\gamma$ (`hi'`), with unique lifting along surjections whose kernel has square zero (`het`), and with fibres over algebraically closed fields described by `hfib`: two values agree if and only if there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ with $g'=\theta_t(\gamma)g$, $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and $\psi'=\mathrm{frobTwist}(-v(\det\iota_0\gamma))\psi$ on every $y\in Onr$ fixed by the Frobenius powers attached to the scalar elements of $\Gamma_t$ lying in the kernel of $\theta_t$.
--
--   **Transport of level structures and of $\Xi$-data (`hC0e`–`hC5`, summarised here).** `hC0e`, `hC0u`: existence and essential uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification. `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`: every pair $(\psi,P)$ over a connected Noetherian base comes from a rigidified curve whose $\Xi$-image has $Onr$-leg $\mathrm{frobTwist}(-v(\det g_0))\psi$ and corresponds to $(\psi,P)$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action; such a pair is unique up to an isomorphism of rigidified curves; and such pairs propagate along base change. `hC2`, `hC2c`: for such a pair, $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ is `ptF` of $(E,P_n)$, and followed by $p$ it is `pt` of $E$. `hC3`: the $\iota_0(\gamma)$-twisted action for $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ is realised by another rigidification on the same curve, the two normalised level-$n$ structures differing by the twist by $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, with the extra level-$\ell$ subgroups matched whenever $e\gamma$ stabilises the corresponding subgroup of $A_0$. `hC4`, `hC4pi`: the analogous statements for the action by $Z^{c}g_0\iota_0(h)g_0^{-1}$ and for $\pi$-translation. `hC5` (the one-leg clause): over an algebraically closed field, if $(E,\varrho)$ and $(E',\varrho')$ correspond to $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ and $E\cong E'$ compatibly with the structures, then there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_t$ carrying $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$ under the twisted action, matching the normalised level-$n$ structures after the twist by $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$ and equating, for each prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in the field, the agreement of extra level-$\ell$ subgroups across the isomorphism with the stability of the corresponding subgroup of $A_0$ under $e\gamma$.
--
--   **The one-leg family at each $\ell$ (`C₀`–`hJOINTs`, `hSTAB`, `hCLe`, `hCLu`).** For each $\ell$, $C_0(\ell)$ is an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$, $A_{0s}(\ell)$ its quotient via $a_s(\ell),a_s'(\ell)$ (`hLIs`), together with an $r^{k_s(\ell)}$-isogeny pair $b_s(\ell),b_s'(\ell)$ preserving the level structure (`hBSs`, `hBSslev`) and the joint normalisation `hJOINTs` pairing the composite $a_s(\ell)$ followed by $b_s(\ell)$ with $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$. `hSTAB`: $e\gamma$ preserves the subgroup $C_0(\ell)$ precisely when $\gamma\in\Gamma_{t,\ell}$. `hCLe`, `hCLu`: the extra level-$\ell$ structure transported from a given one on $A_0$ exists and is unique up to the factorisation predicate it defines.
--
--   **The tower uniformisation (`ΘT`, `hnatT`, `hVT`).** For each $\ell$, $\Theta_{T,\ell}$ sends $B$-points of $(Onr\to_{\mathcal O}-)\times\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to nilpotent points of $g_\ell$, naturally in $B$ (`hnatT`), and `hVT` identifies $\Theta_{T,\ell}(\psi,P)$ with `ptT ℓ` of $(E,C)$ whenever $(E,\varrho)$ is the rigidified curve attached to $(\psi,P)$ as in `hC1e` and $C$ transports $C_0(\ell)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every prime $\ell$ distinct from $r$ and $\bar r$, every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and all $B$-points $x,x'$ of $(Onr\to_{\mathcal O}-)\times\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ such that $x$ is the $\iota_0(s_\ell)$-twisted translate of $x'$ — that is, the $Onr$-leg of $x$ is the $(-v(\det\iota_0(s_\ell)))$-th $Fr$-twist of the $Onr$-leg of $x'$, and the Deligne datum of $x$ is the pullback of that of $x'$ along $\iota_0(s_\ell)^{-1}$ — the nilpotent $B$-point $\Theta_{T,\ell}(x)$ of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ followed by $d_1(\ell)$ coincides with the nilpotent $B$-point $\Theta_f(x',1)$ of $M$ followed by $p$, as $B$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the $d_1$-compatibility of the Čerednik–Drinfeld $r$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve tower: the second degeneracy leg of the Hecke correspondence at a prime $\ell$ away from $r$ and $\bar r$ is computed by translating the rigid-analytic parameter by the Hecke element $s_\ell$. It is one of the input identities for the construction of the uniformising family over the whole tower, used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_towerFamily_liftT_of_rigidifiedToG_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_towerFamily_liftT_of_rigidifiedToG_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5).
